    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: net_sched: hfsc: Fix a potential UAF in hfsc_dequeue() too (CVE-2025-37823)\n\n* kernel: scsi: ses: Fix possible desc_ptr out-of-bounds accesses (CVE-2023-53675)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: Fix out-of-bounds access in ipv6_find_tlv() (CVE-2023-53705)\n\n* kernel: libceph: fix potential use-after-free in have_mon_and_osd_map() (CVE-2025-68285)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
